G1 harness (thermal training in the Brush fork). Results and findings: ../../notes/g1.md.

prepare_g1.py WORKDIR OUT   dataset for Brush from train.py's own scene loading (16-bit scaled
                            temperature targets, frozen eval_views.txt, init.ply, g1.json, gt.npy,
                            brush_args.txt); run with tools/GaussianSplat's venv
run_native.sh DATASET OUT   native brush-cli training with GPU memory sampling (BRUSH=..., ITERS=)
run_browser.mjs             browser training: serves the page (web/), the worker
                            (app/src/stages/train/brush-worker.js), the wasm package and the
                            dataset; drives local headless Chrome (laptop flags) or a remote one
                            over CDP (win11/README); collects renders, PLY, console counts, GPU
                            memory; --trace 1 adds GPU buffer accounting, --shaders 1 saves WGSL
                            exits nonzero unless the run is valid (no GPU/shader error, device loss
                            or worker exception; exactly the frozen renders and a consistent PLY,
                            all tied to this attempt's id; OUT must be new or empty; artifacts of
                            invalid runs are moved to OUT/rejected/)
repeat.sh N PKG DATASET OUT the repeat policy's runs (N valid, at most 3 invalid replaced)
repeat_preflight.sh N PKG DATASET OUT HOST   remote series with a per-attempt adapter preflight
                            (preflight.mjs; failures logged in OUT/ledger.jsonl, not attempts)
score_repeats.py            scores a machine's complete attempt ledger under the repeat policy
                            (5 distinct valid runs, at most 3 invalid attempts, fixed thresholds)
worker_contract_test.mjs    worker failure contract with a mocked brush-js
                            (node --experimental-vm-modules worker_contract_test.mjs)
driver_contract_test.mjs DATASET SCRATCH   driver: fresh output dir, per-attempt verdicts, exact
                            artifact validation (mocked browser)
lifetime_test.sh PKG ...    GPU buffer lifetime regression test (3 x 3500 iterations must stay valid);
                            lifetime-negative-control.patch makes the CubeCL fork fail it
render_ply.py PLY DATASET OUT.npz   held-out renders of any PLY with gsplat, decoded as the viewer
metrics.py score|compare|export     the one scorer (criteria 1-6 and 9 of notes/g1.md); validates
                                    view identities, counts, dimensions, finite values; exits
                                    nonzero on invalid input or a failed criterion
check_loss.py DUMP DATASET  criteria 7-8 against train.py's loss, from the fork's thermal_loss test
                            (THERMAL_LOSS_DUMP=DUMP G1_DATASET=DATASET cargo test -p brush-train
                            --test thermal_loss)
audit_wgsl.py DIR           loop-local uninitialised var audit of captured WGSL
profile_worker.mjs PORT S OUT   CPU profile of the worker (run_browser.mjs --debug-port PORT)
probe/                      minimal WebGPU checks for the laptop (canvas, subgroups, readback)

Worker contract (app/src/stages/train/brush-worker.js): one worker per run, start once, renderEval
and exportPly after 'done', then dispose; any GPU error, shader error or device loss fails the run.

Building the fork: Brush (pinned 1388f74 + ../../app/src/stages/train/brush-patches/brush/*.patch)
with a CubeCL checkout next to it (tracel-ai/cubecl at 467522442c7b + brush-patches/cubecl/*.patch,
as the directory cubecl-fork); then
  cargo build -p brush-js --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --release
  wasm-bindgen --target web --out-dir PKG target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/brush_js.wasm
  cargo build --release -p brush-cli
